# Trivy Ignore File
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Format: <vulnerability-id> [expiration-date | reason]
# Lines starting with '#' are comments
# To ignore a vulnerability: add its ID (e.g., CVE-2024-12345) with optional reason
#
# Example:
# CVE-2024-12345 2026-12-31 # Will be patched in Q4 2026
# CVE-2024-99999          # Known false positive, no patch available
#
# Common categories:
# - test-only dependencies (only in test classpath)
# - build-time only (not included in runtime artifact)
# - false positives (misidentified by scanner)
# - accepted risks (security decision with known tradeoff)
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Example ignored vulnerability (uncomment to use):
# CVE-2024-XXXXX 2026-08-15 # Pending Spring Boot patch in next minor release
